###  http://opendata.inrae.fr/PO2/Ontology/TransformON/c_Yly1iu
<http://opendata.inrae.fr/PO2/Ontology/TransformON/c_Yly1iu> rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                                             rdfs:subClassOf <http://opendata.inrae.fr/PO2/Ontology/TransformON/c_C7XxWI> ,
                                                                             <http://opendata.inrae.fr/PO2/Ontology/TransformON/c_pZjAQu> ;
                                                             <http://opendata.inrae.fr/PO2/core/definitionStatus> "validated" ;
                                                             <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A fibrous material extracted from the phloem of Cannabis sativa plants."@en ;
                                                             <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#editorialNote> "SUBSTANCE::NON FOOD" ;
                                                             <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme> <http://opendata.inrae.fr/PO2/Ontology/TransformON/cs_Main> ,
                                                                                                            <http://opendata.inrae.fr/PO2/Ontology/TransformON/cs_Non_food> ,
                                                                                                            <http://opendata.inrae.fr/PO2/Ontology/TransformON/cs_Substance> ;
                                                             <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "" ;
                                                             <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> ""@de ,
                                                                                                             ""@es ,
                                                                                                             ""@it ,
                                                                                                             "fibre libérienne de chanvre"@fr ,
                                                                                                             "hemp bast fibre"@en ;
                                                             <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> """@en: Depending on variety (or usage type) and planting density, bast fibres typically account for 20-30 % of the stalk.
There are two types of bast fibres: 1)  Primary bast fibres - make up 70-90% of the bast. They are characterized by long length (up to 50 mm), high cellulose (50-70%) and low lignin (about 7%) content. These fibres are the most valuable part of the stalk. 2). Secondary bast fibres - comprise the remaining 10-30% of the bast fibres. They are shorter (approximately 2 mm), more lignified and hence of lower value for some applications (i.e. textile). Low stand density of hemp crop favours development of this type of bast fibre.
""" .


